-  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.header": "Sampling genes with the Isolator",
-  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.header": "Decoding genes with the Sequencer",
-  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.header": "Charging serums with the Polymeriser",
-  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.header": "Applying a serum with the Inoculator",
-  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.header": "High-throughput gene application with the Splicer",
-  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.header": "Revealing genetics with the Analyser",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.header": "Extracting Raw DNA in the Gene Pool",
-  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.header": "Culturing laboratory reagents in the Incubator",
-  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.header": "Adapting organisms with the Acclimatiser",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.header": "Specialising a Forestry Alveary",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_1": "Binnie's Alveary components replace ordinary exterior Alveary blocks. The Forestry multiblock keeps its normal 3×3×3 body and slab cap; only the chosen wall positions change.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_2": "The Mutator consumes mutagen items and multiplies mutation chance, with the resulting modifier capped rather than growing without limit.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_3": "The Frame Housing accepts one Forestry hive frame, contributes that frame's modifiers, and wears the frame while the Alveary runs.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_4": "The Rain Shield lets rain-sensitive bees continue working through bad weather.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_5": "The Lighting block supplies artificial daylight for species that would otherwise stop without suitable light or sky conditions.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_6": "The Stimulator accepts a compatible circuit board and applies its configured bee modifiers while the component is powered.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_7": "The Hatchery can produce larvae from a healthy working queen and stores the resulting larvae internally.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_8": "The Transmission block accepts FE and distributes it to Alveary components that require power, giving powered upgrades a shared supply point.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.header": "Breeding Binnie's genetic flowers",
-  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_1": "Binnie's flowers are genetic organisms. Two flowers can look alike while carrying different active and inactive alleles, so parent choice matters.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_2": "Pollen carries a flower genome. Apply it to another mature flower to pollinate that parent with the donor's genetics.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_3": "Offspring are produced as genetic seeds. Their genomes combine the parents and can contain new inherited traits or mutations, so grow and select the offspring you want to continue breeding.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_4": "Flowerbeds track moisture, acidity, fertility and weedkiller. Use the Soil Meter to inspect the bed, then water or amend the soil instead of guessing what the flower needs.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.header": "Mounting databases on the Lab Stand",
-  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_1": "The Lab Stand is not a processing machine. It is a physical home for Binnie's genetic knowledge databases, keeping frequently used reference tools in the laboratory world.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_2": "Right-click the placed stand with a compatible database to mount it. The mounted item is rendered on the stand instead of disappearing into an invisible inventory.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_3": "Right-click the occupied stand to access the mounted database. Database items can be moved between compatible Lab Stands when you reorganise the laboratory.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_1": "Binnie's Genetics laboratory is a chain of specialised machines. The main route isolates a chromosome sample, sequences it into genetic knowledge, charges an engineered serum, then applies that serum to another organism.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_2": "The Isolator's output is an actual unsequenced Sequence. The Sequencer consumes that component-bearing Sequence with Fluorescent Dye, records the discovered gene for its owner, and returns the Empty Sequencer.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_3": "Use discovered genes in the genetics database to prepare an uncharged Serum or Serum Array. The Polymeriser then adds charges using Polymerising Bacteria and Raw DNA; the item remains a real Serum, not a generic genetic-material placeholder.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_4": "The Inoculator applies a charged Serum to DNA-manipulable stock with Vector Bacteria. JEI's flower example uses genetic Pollen here, because an established Flower is not the manipulable life stage for this operation.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_5": "The Analyser, Gene Pool, Incubator and Acclimatiser handle the supporting laboratory work. Open Ponder on any Genetics machine to start with that machine's focused scene; this overview is now the secondary scene.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_1": "The Isolator takes a genetic individual, an Empty Sequencer, charged Enzyme and Bioethanol. It samples one active or inactive allele into a new unsequenced Sequence.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_2": "This preview now uses the same component-bearing Sequence that JEI displays. The organism can be lost during extraction, so keep valuable breeding stock backed up.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_1": "The Sequencer accepts the real unsequenced Sequence produced by the Isolator and progressively identifies the allele stored in its genetic-sequence component.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_2": "Fluorescent Dye supplies sequencing charge. JEI's Database icon is a reference catalyst rather than a physical Sequencer slot: completion records the discovered gene for the machine owner and returns the Empty Sequencer.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_1": "The Polymeriser charges an actual Serum or Serum Array. This JEI-matched example uses an uncharged Serum Array, a charged Gold Nugget accelerator, Polymerising Bacteria and Raw DNA.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_2": "The output is the same component-bearing Serum Array with one more charge. Repeating the process can bring a serum to sixteen charges; the charged Gold Nugget speeds the operation without changing that result.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_1": "The Inoculator applies genes from a charged Serum to a DNA-manipulable genetic individual. For flowers, JEI correctly demonstrates this with genetic Pollen rather than an established Flower.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_2": "Vector Bacteria is the carrier fluid. Successful processing returns the modified organism and spends one charge from the Serum.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_1": "The Splicer is the aggressive alternative to the Inoculator. It requires a charged Serum Array and a DNA-manipulable individual; this example again uses genetic Pollen, exactly like JEI.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_2": "It applies the array without a Vector Bacteria tank. Processing is much faster, but its FE cost is dramatically higher.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_1": "The Analyser can identify hidden information on an organism or on a Sequence. This focused example uses JEI's real unanalysed Sequence plus DNA Dye.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_2": "The output is the same Sequence with its analysed state changed in the data component. The icon may remain similar, but the stack is no longer the same genetic data.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.text_1": "The Gene Pool destructively processes a real genetic individual with charged Enzyme and Bioethanol, producing Raw DNA as a fluid rather than a genetic-material item.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.text_2": "The individual is not returned. Raw DNA accumulates in the output tank and is later consumed by the Polymeriser.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_1": "The Incubator is a continuous culture machine. Its operations are fluid-and-reagent pairs, so each example below mirrors an actual JEI contract instead of substituting generic laboratory props.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_2": "Sugar in Bacteria produces Enzyme.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_3": "Growth Medium item plus Water produces Growth Medium fluid.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_4": "Wheat in Growth Medium cultures ordinary Bacteria.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_5": "White Dye converts Bacteria into Polymerising Bacteria; Blaze Powder converts it into Vector Bacteria. Both are the exact fluids consumed later in the genetics pipeline.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_1": "The Acclimatiser changes tolerance alleles on the individual itself. Its reagents now come directly from the same examples JEI exposes.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_2": "Powdered Mulch and Powdered Ash steer pH tolerance in opposite directions.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_3": "Lava and Snow adjust temperature tolerance, while Water and Sand adjust humidity tolerance.",
-  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_4": "There is no separate finished-genome item: the output is the same genetic individual with changed tolerance data."
+  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.header": "Genetics Machine Workflow",
+  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.header": "Using the Isolator",
+  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.header": "Using the Sequencer",
+  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.header": "Charging Serums with the Polymeriser",
+  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.header": "Applying Genes with the Inoculator",
+  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.header": "Applying Gene Arrays with the Splicer",
+  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.header": "Analysing Genetic Material",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.header": "Producing Raw DNA",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.header": "Making Genetics Fluids",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.header": "Changing Climate Tolerances",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.header": "Binnie's Alveary Upgrades",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_1": "Binnie's Alveary blocks replace normal blocks in the outside walls of a Forestry Alveary. The Alveary still uses the same 3×3×3 body and slab roof.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_2": "The Mutator consumes mutagen items to increase the chance of bee mutations. The bonus has a limit, so adding more does not increase it forever.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_3": "The Frame Housing holds one Forestry frame and applies that frame's effects to the Alveary. The frame loses durability while the Alveary runs.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_4": "The Rain Shield lets bees that normally stop in the rain keep working through bad weather.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_5": "The Lighting block provides artificial light so bees that need daylight can keep working when the light is too low.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_6": "The Stimulator takes a compatible circuit board and applies its bee modifiers while it has power.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_7": "The Hatchery can produce larvae while a healthy queen is working and stores the larvae inside.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.alveary_components.text_8": "The Transmission block takes FE and shares it with Alveary components that need power.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.header": "Breeding Flowers",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_1": "Binnie's flowers have genes just like bees and trees. Two flowers can look the same but still carry different active and inactive genes, so the parents you use matter.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_2": "Pollen carries the genes of the flower it came from. Use it on another mature flower to pollinate that flower.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_3": "Pollinated flowers can produce Seeds with genes from both parents. Grow the Seeds and keep the offspring with the traits you want.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.botany_breeding.text_4": "Flower soil tracks moisture, acidity, fertility and weedkiller. Use the Soil Meter to check it, then water or fertilise the soil as needed.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.header": "Using the Lab Stand",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_1": "The Lab Stand holds Binnie's genetics Databases and displays the mounted Database on top.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_2": "Right-click the Lab Stand with a compatible Database to place it on the stand.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.laboratory_machine.text_3": "Right-click a Lab Stand with a Database on it to open that Database without carrying it around.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_1": "The main Genetics workflow starts with an organism. First, isolate one of its genes, sequence it, put that gene into a Serum, charge the Serum, then apply it to another organism.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_2": "The Isolator uses an Empty Sequencer to take one gene from the organism. The result is an unsequenced Sequence. The Sequencer reads that Sequence with Fluorescent Dye and returns the Empty Sequencer.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_3": "Once a gene has been discovered, it can be put into a Serum or Serum Array. The Polymeriser charges it with Polymerising Bacteria and Raw DNA so it can be used in the next machines.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_4": "The Inoculator uses Vector Bacteria to apply a charged Serum to an organism. Flowers are modified as Pollen, not as grown Flowers.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genetics_pipeline.text_5": "The other machines handle the rest of the lab work. The Analyser reveals genetic information, the Gene Pool makes Raw DNA, the Incubator makes lab fluids, and the Acclimatiser changes climate tolerances.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_1": "Put an organism, an Empty Sequencer and Enzyme into the Isolator, then supply Bioethanol. It takes one active or inactive gene and produces an unsequenced Sequence.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.isolator.text_2": "The organism can be lost while the gene is being extracted. If it is valuable breeding stock, keep a spare before putting it into the Isolator.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_1": "The Sequencer reads the unsequenced Sequence made by the Isolator. Add Fluorescent Dye and it works through the sample until the gene has been identified.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.sequencer.text_2": "When it finishes, the discovered gene is recorded for you and the Empty Sequencer is returned. A Database can then be used to view the genes you have discovered.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_1": "The Polymeriser adds charges to a Serum or Serum Array. Supply Polymerising Bacteria and Raw DNA, then put the Serum into the machine. A charged Gold Nugget can be added to speed it up.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.polymeriser.text_2": "Each run adds one charge to the Serum. A Serum can hold up to sixteen charges, and using it in another machine spends a charge.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_1": "The Inoculator applies the genes stored in a charged Serum to an organism. Flowers have to be modified as Pollen, not as grown Flowers.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.inoculator.text_2": "Supply Vector Bacteria, the organism and the Serum. When it finishes, the organism comes back with the new gene and the Serum loses one charge.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_1": "The Splicer applies a charged Serum Array to an organism. Like the Inoculator, flowers have to be used as Pollen.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.splicer.text_2": "It does not need Vector Bacteria and works much faster than the Inoculator, but it uses a lot more FE.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_1": "The Analyser reveals genetic information that has not been analysed yet. Put in an organism or an unanalysed Sequence together with DNA Dye.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.analyser.text_2": "The same item comes back analysed. Its genetic information can then be read instead of being hidden.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.text_1": "The Gene Pool breaks down an organism to make Raw DNA. It needs Enzyme and Bioethanol to process the organism.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.genepool.text_2": "The organism is consumed. Raw DNA collects in the output tank and is mainly used to charge Serums in the Polymeriser.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_1": "The Incubator makes several fluids used by the Genetics machines. Give it the right fluid and reagent, and it will keep processing while both are available.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_2": "Sugar and Bacteria make Enzyme.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_3": "A Growth Medium item and Water make Growth Medium fluid.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_4": "Wheat and Growth Medium fluid produce Bacteria.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.incubator.text_5": "White Dye turns Bacteria into Polymerising Bacteria. Blaze Powder turns Bacteria into Vector Bacteria. Both fluids are used later when charging or applying genes.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_1": "The Acclimatiser changes an organism's pH, temperature and humidity tolerances. Put the organism in with a reagent for the tolerance you want to change.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_2": "Powdered Mulch pushes pH tolerance toward acidic conditions. Powdered Ash pushes it toward alkaline conditions.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_3": "Lava and Snow change temperature tolerance, while Water and Sand change humidity tolerance in opposite directions.",
+  "binniecore.ponder.acclimatiser.text_4": "The organism itself is the output. Its tolerance genes are changed instead of creating a separate item."
 }
-- 
2.47.3

